---
import Package from "../layouts/Package.astro";
---

<Package
  slug="ai-code-review/"
  title="AI code review setup"
  description="AI review on every pull or merge request, on GitHub or GitLab, with least-privilege permissions, spend limits and guardrails, tuned to your codebase and handed over."
  lead="AI review that catches real problems before a person looks, runs inside your own GitHub or GitLab, and cannot change anything it should not."
  forWho="Teams whose reviewers are the bottleneck, or who already write code with AI tools"
>
  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>Teams whose reviewers are the bottleneck, and who want a useful first pass on every change.</li>
    <li>Teams already writing code with AI tools, who want the review side to keep up safely.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is included</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>Claude reviewing each change in your CI, using your own Anthropic account and key: on GitHub through Anthropic's official action, and on GitLab through the Claude Code GitLab CI/CD integration, which is currently in beta and maintained by GitLab.</li>
    <li>Review rules built from a shared base and each repository's conventions, tuned over the first changes to keep noise low.</li>
    <li>Findings graded blocking, should-fix or nit, with nits collected into one comment.</li>
    <li>Guardrails: review is comment-only and never approves, changes from outside contributors never reach the model or its key, and timeouts and a monthly spend limit cap the cost.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you receive</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>Review running on the repositories you choose.</li>
    <li>The review rules, documented so your team can adjust them.</li>
    <li>A handover session on tuning and costs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is not included</h2>
  <ul class="excludes">
    <li>Model usage. Anthropic bills your own account directly, so you see and control that cost.</li>
    <li>Ongoing tuning after the handover.</li>
  </ul>
</Package>
